  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Isabel, you're verified. I'm sorry about this.\n\nOrder Q-7901 from Saffron Lane included a paneer tikka masala. The delivery records show the courier picked it up at 6:33 PM and handed it to you in person at 6:50 PM. I can't see from my side how the kitchen mixed up the dish. The records don't show what was packed, so I can't tell you more about the cause.\n\nI can't issue a refund or credit on your account right now. Your account has had 3 refunds in the last 30 days, which triggers an automatic review. While that review is open, I can't refund or credit anything, even for a mistake like this one. I've passed your case to a specialist, with the details of the wrong dish. They'll follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise what the outcome will be.\n\nPlease don't eat the chicken dish. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I see. My order number is 7901, not Q-7901, but I assume that's the same order. I did already eat a few bites before I realized it was chicken, and I've been sick to my stomach since. I'm feeling better now, but that's not something I should have had to deal with.\n\nI'm a Forkful Plus member, and I didn't expect to be told there's no refund at all for a clear mistake like this. I understand you can't change the review from your end, so I'll wait for the specialist to get back to me within 24 hours.\n\nThanks for passing it on. That's all I need for now."
  }
